Wait — but should a bad frame be skipped entirely, including the mesh? Yes: a single bad frame must not reach the mesh or the rig. Skipping is the correct response (the 10Hz feed will be re-supplied with finite values on the next snapshot).

setSelfShipTransform: same — skip.

Helper:
```ts
/** Whether a feed pose is fully finite (the rig's lerp/slerp gives a
 * single non-finite frame no recovery path — see TASK-76.1). */
function poseFinite(
  pos: { x: number; y: number; z: number },
  quat: { x: number; y: number; z: number; w: number },
): boolean {
  return Number.isFinite(pos.x + pos.y + pos.z + quat.x + quat.y + quat.z + quat.w);
}
